<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Maybe I am wrong, but I see you do not find COM (Center Of Mass) in local model coords. You assume that it is always at (0,0,0). Right?</div></blockquote>I believe that's true - it is the problem I've been having with some of my vehicle models which always come out top-heavy and hence roll over too easily.  Being able to adjust the center of mass to be lower to the ground and closer to the front (for most cars for example) would help a lot.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=726">SteveBaker</a> — Sat Sep 30, 2006 1:24 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
